## The Map Room

A human is watching a live map of this repository. Every file an agent reads,
edits or searches lights up; everything nobody has looked at stays dark. When
they want to know what is behind a dark region they click it, and that click
becomes a request you can answer.

**Coverage reports itself.** A hook installed in this repository sends every
file you touch. You never call `report_touch` by hand, and you must not report
a file you did not actually open — the whole value of the map is that it
distinguishes what was looked at from what was not.

**Answering the human's clicks is your job.** At the start of a session, and
whenever the user mentions the map:

```bash
python3 ~/.map-room/map_room_cli.py pending
```

For each request you take:

```bash
python3 ~/.map-room/map_room_cli.py claim <request_id>
# ...read the path named in the request, then...
python3 ~/.map-room/map_room_cli.py complete <request_id> "$(cat <<'EOF'
Sets up how the app gets built and served.
Written so the site works from any web address without extra setup.
Ships the whole app as one big file, which makes the first load slower than it needs to be.
EOF
)"
```

Claim before you explore, so the human sees you picked it up. Always complete
what you claimed — a stuck `claimed` row is worse than a pending one; if you
cannot explore it, complete it saying exactly that.

**The finding is 2 or 3 plain-language lines, never more.** One idea per line,
each starting with a verb, one newline between them — the panel splits on the
newlines. The person reading does not write code and has about five seconds: no
function names, no config keys, no file sizes, no jargon. Say what the file is
*for*, not what it contains. Never fabricate a finding; read the code.

Checking it: `python3 ~/.map-room/map_room_cli.py doctor` prints what this
checkout bound to. `coverage` prints explored versus dark. If `doctor` says
`repo_id : UNBOUND`, this repository has no map and nothing is being reported —
that is deliberate, not a bug.

**If your tool has no hook** and you were told to report yourself, batch one
call per turn with every path you touched:

```bash
python3 ~/.map-room/map_room_cli.py report <path> [<path>...] --quiet
```
